{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"masterful-whimsical-tigermoth","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n`_idempotent_reuse` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:460-508) requires `claim_gate_check` to pass, which requires a certified signature; a BLOCK never signs (__init__.py:711-717). So re-running review-plan on an unchanged blocked plan re-pays the full ~26-call review. Store history shows 117 unrevised BLOCK retries. The sidecar already stamps `verified_at_sha` on every verdict for exactly this purpose (sidecar.py:600-604: \"a BLOCK loop leaves a usable baseline even though a BLOCK never signs\").\n\n## Approach\nAdd a `_verdict_reuse` path beside `_idempotent_reuse`: when no attestation exists, read `sidecar.latest_review_result`; if its `material_fingerprint` equals `attest.current_material_fingerprint` AND its `verified_at_sha` equals the current review code sha AND its verdict is BLOCK, reconstruct the BLOCK verdict from the stored findings/coaching/coverage and return it with `coverage.llm_ran=False, coverage.verdict_reuse=True`, emitting no new sidecar. `--force` bypasses (existing semantics, _cli/_llm_commands.py:470-477). Precedent for the sidecar-baseline comparison: `attest._sidecar_branch_decision` (attest.py:337-380). Alternative rejected: signing BLOCK attestations — would complicate the claim gate's PASS-only trust model for no claim-side benefit.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (new reuse branch), src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py (render reused BLOCK with a \"reused\" marker; exit 1 preserved), tests/llm/test_plan_review_reuse.py (new).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with FakeRunner: unchanged fingerprint+sha after BLOCK -> zero runner invocations, exit 1; changed fingerprint -> full review runs; --force -> full review runs; PASS idempotent path unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Re-running review-plan on identical material_fingerprint and verified_at_sha after a BLOCK performs zero LLM calls (checked: unit test asserts FakeRunner is never invoked and coverage.verdict_reuse is True).\n- [ ] A reused BLOCK exits 1 and renders the stored findings with a \"reused\" marker (checked: CLI renderer unit test).\n- [ ] --force bypasses verdict reuse and runs the full review (checked: unit test asserts runner invoked).\n- [ ] Existing PASS idempotent-reuse tests pass unmodified (checked: pytest run of the existing reuse tests).","id":"7e77-cbe5-5bcf-4096","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-plan re-runs the full LLM review after an unchanged BLOCK (idempotent skip covers PASS only)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384336307581001,"uuid":"71816f8a-4fed-45ca-a8ba-d34860946ce8"}